(VS 2053)</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_delete_perm": [], "users_without_edit_perm": [], "users_without_read_perm": []}, "points": [{"nodegroup_id": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007", "point": {"lat": 27.704856395411866, "lon": 85.30548730800587}, "provisional": false}], "provisional_resource": "false", "resourceinstanceid": "75e409fc-b482-4db0-a7c6-767359e9e09d", "root_ontology_class": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E34_Inscription"}}, {"_id": "7daa0b42-3fe3-4be2-ac3b-462f2a8e9a2b", "_ignored": ["tiles.data.26ac8fa4-af81-11e9-a3d8-0242ac120005.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.66fd9c70-ce1b-11e9-b993-0242ac140002.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.d9f64830-9fc2-11e9-a638-0242ac140004.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.d9f64efc-9fc2-11e9-a638-0242ac140004.en.value.keyword"], "_index": "danam_resources", "_score": 0.0, "_source": {"displaydescription": "<p>The temple known as Gop\u0101le\u015bvara houses a <em>\u015bivali\u1e45ga</em> and is situated on the cremation site of a sage named Gop\u0101la Muni.</p>\n\n<p>The temple features a dome-shaped structure and faces south, located on the path between S\u016bryagh\u0101\u1e6da and Kail\u0101\u015ba. It has a central finial on top of the dome, and although there were originally smaller finials on the four corners of the roof, only two remain (as of June 2023). The temple&#39;s substructure is made of brick and contains the sanctum where a four-faced (<em>caturmukh\u012b</em>) <em>\u015bivali\u1e45ga</em> is enshrined as the main deity. East of the temple is the S\u016bryagh\u0101\u1e6da \u015aiv\u0101laya (<a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/resource/5975d16c-3e6e-48d8-9968-d2413b6e8272\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>PPK1612</strong></a>) ensemble. Inside the sanctum, there is a statue of Hanum\u0101n on the western wall, and a square-shaped hollow space designated for fire oblations. The temple has entrances on all four sides with brick arches (<em>tora\u1e47a</em>).</p>\n\n<p>The exact date of the temple&#39;s construction is unclear, but its architectural style suggests that it was built during the R\u0101\u1e47\u0101 period. The <em>\u015bivali\u1e45ga</em> inside the sanctum was installed around 2022 CE by devotees. The temple premises were neglected and unclean for many decades until devotees took the initiative to clean and develop it into a place suitable for meditation. Unfortunately, the temple was already in a dilapidated state when it was further damaged by the earthquakes in 2015.</p>\n\n<p>No priest is formally appointed for the temple. Instead, a person from the Nep\u0101l\u012b caste has been taking care of the temple for the past 25 years. Due to its serene location, the temple area has become a popular spot for meditation, and the number of people visiting for this purpose has increased over the years. On the auspicious occasion of \u015aivar\u0101tr\u012b, which falls on the 14th day of the dark fortnight of Ph\u0101lguna, a bonfire is set up in front of the temple. Other socio-religious activities are not regularly conducted at this temple.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n", "displayname": "Gop\u0101le\u015bvara Mandira || \u0917\u094b\u092a\u093e\u0932\u0947\u0936\u094d\u0935\u0930 \u092e\u0928\u094d\u0926\u093f\u0930 \u0965 PPK1610 ", "displayname_language": "en", "geometries": [{"geom": {"features": [{"geometry": {"coordinates": [85.34988723831259, 27.71142501494873], "type": "Point"}, "id": "73ee7be3347262b0ff19b975452a2029", "properties": {"nodeId": "d61d682c-b0fe-11e9-8b01-0242ac120006"}, "type": "Feature"}], "type": "FeatureCollection"}, "nodegroup_id": "d61d682c-b0fe-11e9-8b01-0242ac120006", "provisional": false, "tileid": "21f1e17f-d88b-4ff9-9c6d-2f5e5ad2bd7e"}], "graph_id": "f35cc1ca-9322-11e9-a5cc-0242ac120006", "map_popup": [{"language": "en", "value": "<p>The temple known as Gop\u0101le\u015bvara houses a <em>\u015bivali\u1e45ga</em> and is situated on the cremation site of a sage named Gop\u0101la Muni.</p>\n\n<p>The temple features a dome-shaped structure and faces south, located on the path between S\u016bryagh\u0101\u1e6da and Kail\u0101\u015ba. It has a central finial on top of the dome, and although there were originally smaller finials on the four corners of the roof, only two remain (as of June 2023). The temple&#39;s substructure is made of brick and contains the sanctum where a four-faced (<em>caturmukh\u012b</em>) <em>\u015bivali\u1e45ga</em> is enshrined as the main deity. East of the temple is the S\u016bryagh\u0101\u1e6da \u015aiv\u0101laya (<a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/resource/5975d16c-3e6e-48d8-9968-d2413b6e8272\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>PPK1612</strong></a>) ensemble. Inside the sanctum, there is a statue of Hanum\u0101n on the western wall, and a square-shaped hollow space designated for fire oblations. The temple has entrances on all four sides with brick arches (<em>tora\u1e47a</em>).</p>\n\n<p>The exact date of the temple&#39;s construction is unclear, but its architectural style suggests that it was built during the R\u0101\u1e47\u0101 period. The <em>\u015bivali\u1e45ga</em> inside the sanctum was installed around 2022 CE by devotees. The temple premises were neglected and unclean for many decades until devotees took the initiative to clean and develop it into a place suitable for meditation. Unfortunately, the temple was already in a dilapidated state when it was further damaged by the earthquakes in 2015.</p>\n\n<p>No priest is formally appointed for the temple. Instead, a person from the Nep\u0101l\u012b caste has been taking care of the temple for the past 25 years. Due to its serene location, the temple area has become a popular spot for meditation, and the number of people visiting for this purpose has increased over the years. On the auspicious occasion of \u015aivar\u0101tr\u012b, which falls on the 14th day of the dark fortnight of Ph\u0101lguna, a bonfire is set up in front of the temple. Other socio-religious activities are not regularly conducted at this temple.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_delete_perm": [], "users_without_edit_perm": [], "users_without_read_perm": []}, "points": [{"nodegroup_id": "d61d682c-b0fe-11e9-8b01-0242ac120006", "point": {"lat": 27.71142501494873, "lon": 85.34988723831259}, "provisional": false}], "provisional_resource": "false", "resourceinstanceid": "7daa0b42-3fe3-4be2-ac3b-462f2a8e9a2b", "root_ontology_class": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E71_Man-Made_Thing"}}, {"_id": "02919234-68aa-4fa0-bffb-6723d49e8988", "_ignored": ["tiles.data.c0dc905a-9910-11ea-9766-0242ac130005.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.2591e954-9a98-11ea-82af-0242ac130005.en.value.keyword"], "_index": "danam_resources", "_score": 0.0, "_source": {"displaydescription": "KAT1230_I_005", "displayname": "KAT1230_I_005 A stone\u00a0inscription at\u00a0T\u0101r\u0101 Nani,\u00a0Itum\u0323 Ba\u0304ha\u0304h\u0323, Kathmandu re the construction of Dharmadh\u0101tujin\u0101laya Caitya (C)\u00a0(NS 1079)", "displayname_language": "en", "geometries": [{"geom": {"features": [{"geometry": {"coordinates": [85.3080720527239, 27.70706437068668], "type": "Point"}, "id": "a27838e7-8a05-4db1-8a05-5c6470716119", "properties": {"nodeId": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007"}, "type": "Feature"}], "type": "FeatureCollection"}, "nodegroup_id": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007", "provisional": false, "tileid": "83785bae-5eb4-4a06-886d-6eb292a28f06"}], "graph_id": "6215ee02-990d-11ea-9766-0242ac130005", "map_popup": [{"language": "en", "value": "<p>A stone&nbsp;inscription at&nbsp;T\u0101r\u0101 Nani,&nbsp;Itum\u0323 Ba\u0304ha\u0304h\u0323, Kathmandu re the construction of Dharmadh\u0101tujin\u0101laya Caitya (C)&nbsp;(NS 1079)</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_delete_perm": [], "users_without_edit_perm": [], "users_without_read_perm": []}, "points": [{"nodegroup_id": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007